  "reason": "Pins, current prompt, one-call provenance, and generic mechanics pass: 256x192, one 16,361-pixel component, 332‰ coverage, anchor contact, S detector only, clear corners, and no chroma. Visual semantics fail. The staircase climbs toward a broad upper-right top landing, but S must climb left/down to a lower-left high landing with risers facing upper-right; its low tail merely touching the S band does not establish the required elevation orientation. A tall exposed side/riser mass also runs nearly its full length and reads at 64x48 runtime as a raised stair platform or retaining-wall block, not a compact 36–48-pixel bed with shallow discrete risers. Regenerate with the high landing lower-left, no continuation through the low anchor, and only shallow bed support.",
